I have everything I need. `Get_file_last_version`, `fetch`, etc. let me confirm the profile ("member") shape and the existing teams store. Now let me deliver the functional mockup per the Mockups profile.

---

## Direct Recommendation

Build a **Team Workspace** that reframes each *profile* as a **business "team member"** (AI teammate). Managers see a roster of people-like cards grouped by **team/department**, click a member to edit their **About**, **Persona & instructions**, **Capabilities**, and **Advanced** details — all in plain business language with the technical concepts (regex, tools, API) tucked behind an "Advanced" progressive-disclosure section.

**Terminology mapping (key to making it non-technical):**

| Current (technical) | New (business) |
|---|---|
| Profile | Team member |
| `category` (assistant/agent/file…) | Business role (Assistant, Agent, Reviewer, File Specialist, Team Lead) |
| `content` (system prompt) | Persona & instructions |
| `llm_model` | AI engine |
| `tools` | Skills |
| `use_knowledge` | Access to company knowledge |
| `file_match` (regex) | File trigger (Advanced) |
| `api_settings.active` | Shareable via API (Advanced) |
| `profiles` (linked) | Works with (other members) |

---

## 1 · Screen / Flow Outline

- **App shell** — left icon rail (Team · Activity · Knowledge · Settings) + topbar.
- **Team roster (main)** — stats strip (Members · Teams · Skills · Knowledge-enabled), search, role filter, team filter, sort, view switch (**By team** grid ⇄ **Board**), *Add member*.
- **Member card** — avatar, name, role badge, team chip, tagline, indicators (knowledge / #skills / engine). Hover actions: *Edit*, *Delete*. Board cards are **draggable between teams**.
- **Member editor (right drawer)** — tabs:
  1. **About** — name, role, team, avatar, tagline.
  2. **Persona** — plain-language instructions editor + template chips + live preview.
  3. **Capabilities** — AI engine, company knowledge toggle, skills (tool) picker.
  4. **Advanced** — works-with members, file trigger, API sharing, delete.
- **Add member modal** — start from a template + name/role/team.
- **Delete confirm modal**, **toasts**, and a reviewer **state switcher** (Ready · Loading · Empty · Error).

## 2 · Mock API Contract

| Method | Endpoint | Payload → Returns |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/api/profiles` | — → `Member[]` |
| GET | `/api/profiles/:name` | — → `Member` |
| POST | `/api/profiles` | `Member` → `Member` (201) |
| DELETE | `/api/profiles/:name` | — → `{ ok:true }` |
| GET | `/api/profiles/tools` | — → `{ name, description, tags[] }[]` |
| GET | `/api/projects/ai/models` | — → `{ name, ai_provider, tier }[]` |

`Member` mirrors the real profile shape: `{ id, name, category, avatar, llm_model, description, content, file_match, profiles[], tools[], use_knowledge, api_settings:{active,modelName,modelDescription}, teamId }` (mock adds `teamId` for grouping).

