---

## What's mocked

- **Endpoints:** `GET/POST/DELETE /api/profiles(/:id)` and `GET /api/profiles/tools`, `GET /api/projects/ai/models` — all served by `mockFetch()` with **simulated latency (180–440 ms)** and an optional forced `?_fail=1`.
- **Seed data:** 8 members (mirroring real profile fields), 4 teams, 12 skills, 4 AI engines.
- **Extension:** a `teamId` field groups members into teams. Real profiles don't have this yet — the eventual Vue view needs a `team`/`department` attribute (or a small team config).
- **States reachable:** the *State* dropdown in the toolbar switches **Ready · Loading (skeleton) · Empty · Error**.
- **Persistence:** mutations are stored in `localStorage['mock.codx.teamView']`; the ↻ button in the left rail resets it.
- **Not wired:** real auth, real network, and the chat-based prompt editor (this mock uses a direct persona textarea instead of `ChatView`).

## Try it — walk these paths

1. **Arrange a team:** switch the layout to **Board** → drag *Liam O'Brien* from *Customer Support* into *Engineering* → a toast confirms and the grid view reflects the new team.
2. **Edit a persona:** click any member → **Persona** tab → click a *template chip* → watch the live preview update → **Save member**.
3. **Capabilities:** open a member → **Capabilities** → toggle *Access to company knowledge* and add a couple of **Skills** → the card's indicator counts change on close.
4. **Add a member:** *Add member* → name it, pick template *Support Agent* → it appears under the chosen team.
5. **Delete flow:** hover a card → trash icon → confirm dialog → toast.
6. **States:** use the *State* dropdown to preview **Loading**, **Empty**, and **Error** (and hit **Retry** on the error screen).
7. **Persistence:** reload the page — your edits are still there; press the rail's ↻ to reset.

## Run note

**Open `team-view.html` directly in a browser — no server or build step required.**

---

## Design specifications

| Area | Decision |
|---|---|
| Layout | 64 px icon rail · fluid main · roster grid (2–4 cols) · board columns 288 px · right drawer 480 px |
| Colors | Canvas `#0b0b0d`, surfaces `#16161a/#1f1f24`, primary `#6366f1`; roles carry their own accent (indigo/violet/cyan/blue), teams carry a strip color |
| Typography | System stack · H1 18px/700 · body 15px · labels 12px/600 · captions 11px — one scale, no surprises |
| Spacing | 8 px grid (gaps 8/12/16/24) · card radius 14px · control radius 10px |
| States | hover lifts cards (`translateY(-2px)`), focus ring `2px #818cf8` **always visible**, `active:scale(.97)`, disabled `opacity .45` |

## Accessibility checklist

- [x] Semantic `<nav> <main> <aside role=dialog> <article>` — no clickable `<div>`s masquerading as buttons (cards use `role="button"` + `tabindex` + Enter/Space handling).
- [x] Visible focus ring on every interactive element; `Esc` closes drawer/modal; focus moves into the editor and modal on open.
- [x] Icon-only controls carry `aria-label`; toggles/checkboxes are real inputs with labels.
- [x] Toasts use `aria-live="polite"`; the error screen uses `role="alert"`.
- [x] Text contrast ≥ 4.5:1 on all surfaces; `prefers-reduced-motion` disables animation.
- [x] Status is never color-only (role badges include an icon + label).

## Anti-patterns to avoid

- ❌ **Exposing the raw system prompt as "content"** to managers — always frame it as *Persona & instructions* with templates.
- ❌ **Flat, techno-centric labels** (`file_match`, `agent-validator`) in the main flow — bury them one level deep in *Advanced*.
- ❌ **A single happy path** — loading/empty/error are first-class and must be reproduced in the Vue port.

## Implementation steps (next, in Vue 3)

1. **Data:** add `teamId` (or a `teams` config) to the profile model on the backend; expose `/api/teams`.
2. **View:** create `src/views/TeamView.vue` (or repurpose `ProfileView.vue`) reusing the roster/board split above.
3. **Components:** extract `MemberCard.vue`, `MemberEditorDrawer.vue` (tabs *About/Persona/Capabilities/Advanced*), `AddMemberDialog.vue` — reuse existing `ChatLLMModelSelector` for the AI-engine picker and `ChatProfileSelector` for *Works with*.
4. **Store:** map these to `$storex.profiles` (list/save/delete) so the mock's `mockFetch` calls map 1:1 to `project.$api.profiles.*`.
5. **Keep the persona editor** wired to `ChatView` in the real build, but keep the plain textarea as the default for non-technical managers.

